{"id": "86318", "name": "Diff_Product_2", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p>Find \\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}\\] where \\[ y(x)= {{CT:0}}\\]</p>\n<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>", "generalfeedback": "<p>In order to solve this problem we will have to use the product rule \\(\\frac{d}{dx}(fg) = \\frac{df}{dx}\\cdot g+f\\cdot\\frac{dg}{dx}\\) as follows:</p>\n<p><br /> Let \\(f(x) = \\sin({{CT:1}})\\mbox{ and }g(x) = \\displaystyle\\frac{1}{\\cos({{CT:1}})+{{CT:2}}}\\) <br /> \\[\\begin{array}{rcl}\\displaystyle \\frac{d}{d{{CT:1}}}\\left({{CT:0}}\\right) &amp; =&amp; \\frac{d}{d{{CT:1}}}({{CT:3}})\\cdot\\left({{CT:4}}\\right)+\\frac{d}{d{{CT:1}}}\\left({{CT:4}}\\right)\\cdot({{CT:3}}) \\\\ &amp; =&amp; ({{CT:5}})\\cdot{{CT:4}}+({{CT:3}})\\cdot{{CT:6}} \\\\ &amp; =&amp; = {{CT:7}}+{{CT:8}} \\end{array}\\]</p>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "diff", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "Diff", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "correctanswer", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "wronganswer1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-T ", "feedback": "<p>To differentiate a product use the rule \\[\\frac{d}{dx}(fg) = \\frac{df}{dx}\\cdot g+f\\cdot\\frac{dg}{dx}.\\] You cannot get the derivative of a product by multiplying the derivatives.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "Result-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "wronganswer2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-2-T ", "feedback": "<p>You appear to have applied the product rule incorrectly. It is \\[\\frac{df}{dx}\\cdot g+f\\cdot\\frac{dg}{dx},\\] not \\[f\\cdot\\frac{df}{dx}+g\\cdot\\frac{dg}{dx}.\\]</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "penalty": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-2-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["correctanswer", "dfp", "dfp1", "dfp2", "n1", "p", "pp1", "pp2", "v", "wronganswer1", "wronganswer2"], "nvariants": 9}